    "reasoning": "The first fourteen answers agree with their own captured solutions. Rate calculations give 280/70=4 ft/s; 602/4=150.5 ft/min; 55×3=165 miles; (135/30)×18=81 cm; 396/(315/35)=44 s; and 3960/660=6 min. Triangle areas use one-half base times perpendicular height: 4×6/2=12; 5×12/2=30 m²; 13²/2=84.5; and 10²/2=50. For q-87910, CD=2×42/7=12 cm, so ABC has area 5×12/2=30 cm². For q-117356, AC=2×64/8=16 m, giving AM=16−11=5 m. Acceleration units are length/time². For q-59502 and q-59749, acceleration is respectively (20−0)/10=2 m/s² and (12−2)/4=2.5 m/s². Both captured calculations correctly express these units, but their concluding answers and every current choice instead square the entire velocity unit, (m/s)², which has dimensions m²/s². These are authored unit errors. MA's intended numerical choices are option 2 in both cases, but neither field offers a dimensionally correct choice, so correct_option is null. No submitted grades were supplied.",
